rks. Members of SUSO also play for Setnor's Opera Workshop production every January.\n\nThe orchestra is directed by James R. Tapia, director of orchestral activities at the Setnor School of Music.\n\nFaculty Contact\n\nJames R. Tapia\n\nThe SU Wind Ensemble is the premiere concert wind organization at Syracuse University. The Wind Ensemble has performed at major conferences and has featured guest conductors and soloists from around the world. Recent guest conductors include Miguel Etchegoncelay (France), Laura Cmet (Argentina), Shanti Simon, and Paula Crider. Over the past several decades, the SU Wind Ensemble has"
