    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Greta Gerwig and Noah Baumbach\ndate: 2023-06-01\n---\nJeff Kravitz/FilmMagic, Inc/Getty Images\n\nIt's hard to predict how celebrity couples will tie the knot these days. Some will go the private, hush-hush route like Kate Bosworth and Justin Long. Others may choose to be more forthcoming like Sofia Richie and Elliot Grainge's multi-day, Chanel-filled extravaganza in the South of France. Or perhaps they may want something more exhilarating a la Chris Appleton and Lukas Gage's whirlwind Vegas ceremony officiated by Kim Kardashian. No matter the manner (or if they even make their marriage public knowledge), continue to check back here for every celebrity wedding in 2023.\n\nGreta Gerwig and Noah Baumbach have officially tied the knot after twelve years of dating. Per People, the couple got married at New York City Hall. Gerwig's reps confirmed the marriage, though added no other details.\n\nIt's been a successful year both personally and professionally for the couple, who first met back in 2010 while working on the film Greenberg and began dating one year later. The pair would go on to collaborate on Frances Ha and co-wrote the blockbuster movie, Barbie, and quietly welcomed their second son back in July.\n\n\"He's a little Schmoo, that's very much his energy,\" Gerwig told Elle UK. \"He's a wise little baby. The little guy is sleeping through the night. But I'm still doing that thing where I wake up, every hour to 90 minutes, and just hover. You just keep wanting to look at that baby. So I'm slightly in a twilight state.\"\n\nThe couple were also nominated for two Academy Awards back in 2020 (Gerwig for adapting Little Women, and Baumbach for writing Marriage Story). Around the time, Baumbach described their working relationship. \"When we write together, I'm always trying to impress her. I feel like I write better because I work at it harder, I want her to be impressed,\" he said.\n\nVanessa Hudgens was spotted on a beach in Mexico wearing a white dress which, in celebrity world, usually means one thing. Per People, the actress and baseball player Cole Tucker said \"I do\" on December 2nd.\n\nAlthough not much is known about the specifics of the ceremony, Hudgens wore a casual, strapless white dress. The ceremony was also attended by Hudgen's High School"
