    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Before they were famous: 35 celebrities who were models before becoming stars\ndate: 2023-08-02\n---\nOver the years, we have assembled these old pictures of celebrities from before they were famous. In most cases, their names did not appear because it was long before they could demand higher rates as well-known names endorsing a product.\n\nOf course, the model-to-actor/actress career switch and rise to stardom isn't just a coincidence \u2014 it's usually part of a long journey, which requires a mix of talent, looks and luck. It also takes a discerning eye to find faces with the perfect blend of qualities that will make them recognizable even decades later.\n\nSome of the top talent scouts and photographers can sometimes make the stars align \u2014 almost literally \u2014 and wind up with two up-and-comers in the same photoshoot! Here's an example of that from the early 80s, featuring actress Phoebe Cates on the left, and singer Whitney Houston in the middle:\n\nFrom model to actor: The magic transformation of these celebrities from photoshoots to film fame\n\nThe modeling industry can be an excellent training ground for aspiring stars. Beyond providing a platform to showcase physical appeal, it offers exposure to high-profile clientele, photographers, and industry insiders.\n\nIt's a fascinating journey, marked by perseverance and opportunity, that continues to bring fresh faces into the limelight \u2014 from the pages of fashion magazines to the big screen \u2014 shaping the entertainment industry's landscape in unexpected and fascinating ways.\n\nBelow, check out some long-forgotten photos of today's celebrities who started out as models! (We know there are more out there. Who did we miss? Please let us know in the comments!)\n\nDON'T MISS: \ud83d\udcf7 40+ adorable celebrity baby pictures from before these stars were famous\n\nBEFORE THEY WERE FAMOUS: MODELS OF THE 1960s & 1970s\n\nYoung Candice Bergen before she was an actress\n\nAs someone who had grown up in the limelight as the daughter of Edgar Bergen (of ventriloquist fame), young Candice Bergen became the face of many different brands, and appeared in hundreds of different outfits for fashion magazines.\n\nThis early foray into the public eye and her inherent grace helped the future Murphy Brown star navigate a successful transition to both the small and big screens. Her modeling days were instrumental in developing her poised persona, a quality that later became her trademark in the entertainment industry.\n\nCandice Bergen for Bon"
