    "snippet": "---\ntitle: Celebrities Who Are Siblings\nauthor: Sarah Ng\ndate: 2024-07-08\n---\nIt runs in the family\n\nHollywood is home to many talented siblings who have taken the entertainment industry by storm. From acting dynasties to musical prodigies, these siblings share a family bond and a dedication to their craft, making show business truly a family affair.\n\nCole And Dylan Sprouse\n\nThese siblings can thank television for their fame. At just 11 years old, the brothers starred in the Disney Channel's The Suite Life of Zack and Cody, which ran for three seasons from 2005 to 2008. They then kept the momentum with the spinoff The Suite Life on Deck from 2008 to 2011. Since then, Cole earned acting chops on Riverdale and Dylan appeared in films like After We Collided.\n\nFinneas O'Connell And Billie Eilish\n\nBillie Eilish's music has earned her five Grammy awards, but she couldn't have done it without the help of her brother, Finneas O'Connell. After releasing songs online, Eilish catapulted to fame with \"Bad Guy\" with O'Connell co-writing many of Eilish's biggest hits. When not helping his sister write award-winning music, O'Connell is an actor.\n\nCasey And Ben Affleck\n\nThese Oscar-winning brothers both began their careers as child stars. Ben is most famous for his roles in Armageddon, Pearl Harbor, and Gone Girl. And don't forget his Academy Awards for writing and producing Good Will Hunting, which he co-wrote with longtime friend Matt Damon, and Argo, which he produced. Casey starred in Good Will Hunting and the Ocean's Eleven series and Manchester by the Sea, which won him an Academy Award in 2017. Ben is three years older than Casey.\n\nJenna And Barbara Bush\n\nThese twins are the daughters of President George W. Bush and granddaughters of the late President George H.W. Bush. Their political lineage has made them media darlings since they were babies. Now that their dad is no longer the leader of the free world, Jenna has become a journalist, author, and TV host while Barbara has pursued social activism working with nonprofits. The sisters have also written books together, including Sisters First in 2017.\n\nBeau And Jeff Bridges\n\nSons of Hollywood legend Lloyd Bridges, both Beau and Jeff have become icons in their own right. Jeff's credits include The Big Leb"
