was the first time metric units rather than imperial units were used in all events and was the first time the Games were held in Scotland.\n\n-\n\n1970\n\nThe first international tourism figures for Scotland were released:\n\nTrips Nights Spend 0.62 million 8.5 million \u00a3262 million -\n\n1972\n\nIn March, April and May, the \"A Taste of Scotland\" pilot scheme was developed to promote Scottish food"
