    "snippet": "---\ntitle: The Murdoch Family: All About the Real-Life People Who Inspired 'Succession'\nauthor: Lynsey Eidell\ndate: 2024-09-17\n---\nAn elderly media tycoon with several grown children in consideration to be his successor: What sounds like the plot of Succession is actually the reality for Rupert Murdoch and his six children.\n\nBut unlike in the critically acclaimed series, Rupert's eldest son, Lachlan, will take over the 93-year-old's business empire, Fox Corp and News Corp.\n\nRupert has been married four times and has six children with three of his wives: Prudence (with his first wife Patricia Booker); Elisabeth, Lachlan and James (with his second wife Anna Torv); and Chloe and Grace (with his third wife, Wendi Deng). After divorcing his fourth wife, Jerry Hall, in August 2022, the media tycoon announced his engagement to Ann Lesley Smith on March 20, 2023 (the pair called off their engagement just a few weeks later).\n\nOver the years, there was public speculation about each of his four older children and their potential to be the next leader of the conservative media empire. But Rupert himself was notorious for avoiding the topic: \"Let the chips fall where they will,\" he once said, according to The Irish Times.\n\nIn April 2023, Vanity Fair published an article indicating that Rupert believed a \"Darwinian struggle\" would produce the most capable successor. \"He pitted his kids against each other their entire lives. It's sad,\" a person close to the family told the outlet.\n\nSince stepping down as chairman of Fox and News Corp. in November 2023, Rupert has requested that the Murdoch Family Trust, which dates back to 1999, be amended to give Lachlan total control and voting power without his siblings' interference upon his death.\n\nAs a result, a fierce court battle between Rupert and three of his children \u2014 Prudence, Elisabeth and James \u2014 began on Sept. 16, 2024. The trio are fighting for equal voting rights on the board of News Corp and Fox News as laid out in the current trust.\n\nFrom multiple marriages to media moves and many grandchildren, here is a closer look at the powerful Murdoch family and their complicated dynamic.\n\nRupert Murdoch\n\nMedia mogul Rupert Murdoch was born on March 11, 1931, in Australia. His business empire began when he was just 22 years old and his father, Sir Keith Murdoch, unexpectedly"
