    "snippet": "---\ntitle: 51 Celebrities You Didn't Know Were Athletes in High School\ndate: 2020-01-29\n---\n1Amy Adams\n\nSteve Granitz//Getty Images Amy danced and did track in high school, and she was especially passionate about dance. \"I didn't go to the university because there weren't options in my family. And I stopped the athletic options. I was supposed to stick with track because I was really quick and I could run fast, but I told them, 'I want to dance,'\" she said to the Hollywood Reporter in 2008.\n\n2Phil Robertson\n\nCharles Norfleet//Getty Images The star of A&E's Duck Dynasty was an athlete growing up before hitting reality TV. According to ESPN, he played football as the quarterback for Louisiana Tech. Now he's just hunting down game.\n\nAdvertisement - Continue Reading Below\n\n3Joel McHale\n\nFrazer Harrison//Getty Images While at the University of Washington, the comedian, actor, and TV host was a tight end for the football team! So, he played during college years. Yet apparently he was not very good, so it's wise he chose a different career path.\n\n4Jon Stewart\n\nKevin Winter//Getty Images The comedian played as a winger on the William & Mary men's soccer team back in college and even made it to the varsity team after beginning as a walk-on. He even helped his team reach the NCAA tournament by scoring a winning goal. \"He was a really good player,\" said his coach. \"He wasn't the best player, but he was a good player. His journey speaks to the type of person he is. He's very hard working and not easily discouraged.\"\n\nAdvertisement - Continue Reading Below\n\n5Forest Whitaker\n\nMike Coppola//Getty Images Whitaker played football during high school and went on to California State Polytechnic University in Pomona by way of a football scholarship. Yet, he got a back injury and decided to transfer to the University of Southern California on a music scholarship, instead.\n\n6Matthew Fox\n\nMario Perez//Getty Images The Lost star got a rude awakening about his football skills, and clearly he was just led to acting instead. He actually lost 44 straight games during his college football career (yikes). He had a 2-38 record when he played wide receiver for Columbia.\n\nAdvertisement - Continue Reading Below\n\n7Emma Watson\n\nDia Dipasupil//Getty Images The Little Women actress was actually an excellent field hockey player when she studied at Brown University."
