nditional responsibilities. The auditor must fulfill responsibilities of this type in all cases in which the circumstances exist to which the requirement applies. Failure to discharge an unconditional responsibility is a violation of the relevant standard and Rule 3100.\n\n(2) Presumptively Mandatory Responsibility: The word \"should\" indicates responsibilities that are presumptively mandatory. The auditor must comply with requirements of this type"
